  "result": "Fixed. `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py` now gives a child context its own section of the parent's `default_map`, keyed by `info_name`. Before, it inherited the whole parent map, so `{'foo': {'name': 'changed'}}` never matched the `name` option.\n\nThe change is `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. If the parent has no entry for that name, the child gets `None`.\n\nI added `test_group_default_map_subcommand_section` to `tests/test_commands.py`. It checks that `foo` prints `changed` with the default map and `normal` without it. Running `python -m pytest tests/test_commands.py tests/test_defaults.py -q` gives 145 passed. I did not run the full suite.",
